# Cache

## Framework semantics

CakePHP `Cache` engines are configured in `config/app.php`. Caching is an optimization with an invalidation story — not a substitute for correct query ownership or fixing N+1.

## Required behavior

- Configure engines/prefixes in config; use `Cache::write/read/remember` (or project wrappers) consistently.
- Cache derived/expensive reads with explicit keys and TTL; document invalidation on writes.
- Do not cache authorization decisions in a way that outlives permission changes without invalidation.
- Prefer fixing queries before adding Redis for a single hot path.

## Anti-patterns

- Caching as a band-aid for fat controllers / N+1
- Unbounded keys without prefixes colliding across apps/envs
- Do not invent Laravel Cache facades as CakePHP defaults

## Review checklist

- [ ] Engine config is environment-aware
- [ ] Write paths invalidate or version keys
- [ ] Authz not stale-cached unsafely
